raspberry-flash (0.1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Added the raspberry-flash command line tool: it writes a Raspberry Pi OS
    image (--image) onto an SD card (--device) with rpi-imager, and reports
    the outcome through its exit code.
  * Added the configuration of the Raspberry Pi on its first boot, without
    screen nor keyboard:
    - hostname (--hostname);
    - user account (--username), replacing the default user of the image;
    - WiFi network (--wifi-ssid, --wifi-country), left unconfigured when no
      SSID is given;
    - timezone (--timezone) and keyboard layout (--keymap);
    - SSH server, enabled with password login, or restricted to a public key
      when one is given (--ssh-pubkey).
  * Added the reading of the passwords from the RASPBERRY_FLASH_PASSWORD_USER
    and RASPBERRY_FLASH_PASSWORD_WIFI environment variables, so that they
    never appear on a command line. The WiFi one is only required with
    --wifi-ssid. The user password is stored on the SD card as a SHA-512 hash,
    never in clear.
  * Added --log-level to choose the verbosity of the logs written to stderr,
    --help and --version.
  * Added the Debian packaging: make build freezes the application with
    PyInstaller and builds a standalone .deb with dpkg-deb, for the
    architecture of the machine building it. The bundled interpreter means the
    target needs no system Python, and the package declares its runtime
    dependencies (rpi-imager, openssl, libc6, zlib1g).
  * Added the development environment: uv with a pinned, uv-managed CPython
    3.13, hatchling build backend and a Makefile exposing install-deps, lint,
    format, test, build and clean.

 -- Romain Groux <romaingroux@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:52:27 +0100
